# Markdown: an image alone in its paragraph becomes an Image, and one inside a sentence is as tall as the letters.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Markdown · Images
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For element: Image
			Box:
				Width: 50mm
				Margin: 0 0 10 0
	Section:
		Text: Markdown
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Images
		Paragraph: `![alt](path)` alone in its paragraph is an `Image`, with the text in brackets as its `Alt`. Its size comes from `For element: Image`. Inside a sentence it is an inline image, as tall as the letters, and with empty brackets it is decorative.
			Style: intro
		Markdown:
			Content >>
				![Walnut chair with a wool seat](examples/catalog/silla.jpg)

				The menu of the day carries the emblem ![Emblem of the restaurant](examples/menu/emblem.svg) of the house,
				and the planner icon ![](examples/planner/icon.png) in the same line is decorative.
